SOUNDDVR device-3 per-tick VOICE/ENVELOPE ADVANCE (FUN_0000_0a28, asm 0xa28-0xa9d) reconstructed --
the OPL A0/B0 FNUM feed the menu melody was missing (docs/audio.md §17).

The 42 device-3 note posts KEY-ON via 10e3 but their PITCH is never programmed: the frequency method
FUN_0000_10a6 (writes OPL A0 fnum-lo / B0 block+fnum-hi from the table cs:0x9dd) was NEVER CALLED, so
every note keyed on at fnum 0 -> near-silent (peak 330 vs oracle 6714).  10a6's only dispatcher is the
per-tick voice-envelope advance loop at driver 0xa3a (inside FUN_0000_0a28): it walks the 10 voices,
accumulates each voice's current note = voice[0xc2] (base, set on key-on by 0aa7) + voice[0xb8] (bend)
+ the note-stream delta at voice[voice*2+0x90], and when the note CHANGES from voice[0xcc] it dispatches
slot4 [ds:0x1b3] = 10a6 to reprogram the fnum.  In the real driver 0a28 is called from the timer ISR at
cs:0x1d2 via `call [cs:0x5c2]` (the device-3 config at 0x95b sets [cs:0x5c2]=0x0a28); the port drives it
per PIT tick from the shim (fist_sb.c) -- we own INT-8.

Ghidra base-lost the whole body: the entry `mov cs:0x831,ds` sets ds = the driver data seg, but every
ds: access decompiled to a bare offset, AND the two indirect method dispatches were mis-based to the
ENGINE DGROUP (g_mem+0x1c1b3 / 0x1c189) instead of the driver-DS live method slots (0x1b3 = freq slot4,
0x189 = tail slot1).  Reconstructed asm-verified vs re_out/fist_snd_image.bin (driver-DS = DAT_0000_0831
<<4, the patch-353/354 class), 1:1 control flow:

  a28: mov cs:0x831,ds            ; ds = driver data seg
  a2d: cmpw [0xe],0 ; jne 0xc39   ; per-tick housekeeping (0c39) when [ds:0xe]!=0
  a37: mov bx,9                   ; 10 voices, 9..0
  a3a: mov ah,[bx+0xc2]           ; base note
  a3e: cmpb [bx+0x111],0 ; dec ; ==2 -> ah=0; ch=bl(voice); call 0aa7 (duration-expiry release)
  a59: add ah,[bx+0xb8]           ; + pitch bend
  a5d: shl bx,1 ; walk [bx*2+0x90] note stream (0x80=end, 0x81=loop to [+0xa4], else ah+=byte, advance)
  a83: shr bx,1
  a87: cmp [bx+0xcc],ah ; jne -> [bx+0xcc]=ah; ch=bl; call *[ds:0x1b3] = 10a6 FREQUENCY (A0/B0 fnum)
  a97: dec bx ; jns 0xa3a
  a9a: jmp *[ds:0x189]            ; tail slot1 = 10a5 (ret)

Reached only under FIST_SB (device 3 selected + the shim drives 0a28 per tick); the default boot never
dispatches here -> zero effect on the 26 video flows.

